\begin_layout Plain Layout
\begin_inset Caption Standard

\begin_layout Plain Layout
Conditionally punishing kernel in discrete space.
 If the solution is closer than 0.5 to the solution, it will not be penalised
 as correct, MAE otherwise.
 The candidate consisting of just one node cheats itself a low error by
 concentrating on minimising wrong decisions.
\end_layout

\end_inset


\end_layout

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
This kernel has been tested to give preference to scarce wrong decisions
 in case of wrong decisions, thus allowing convergence towards an optimum.
 If the limit value corresponds to the desired result, it is assigned to
 it accordingly, otherwise the error is calculated.
 If the limit value corresponds to the desired result, it is assigned to
 it accordingly, otherwise the error is calculated.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
\begin_inset Formula $d_{conditional}(x_{i},x_{j})=\sum\begin{cases}
0 & d(x_{ik},x_{jk})<0.5\\
d(x_{ik},x_{jk}) & \text{otherwise}
\end{cases}$
\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Although such a procedure seems to be intuitive, in GP optimisation it leads
 to the fact that correctly found results are only very vaguely met and
 instead only the error is optimised for the wrong decisions.
 The regression error thus loses its function as a distance measure.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Section
Phenotypic Analysis with Regression on the Origin Policy
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
As a measure of complexity in the evolutionary process, the TED controls
 the extent of changes to the programme, the genotypes, but can also have
 a corresponding effect on the phenotype.
 Because both the (see results), because the structure must often be based
 on the already functioning structures while improving the regression error.
 If one wants to analyse the deviation in phenotype, there is the option
 to add the regression error to the expert policy as a factor.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Changes should be made primarily in the direction of the target solution,
 otherwise they are obviously uncertain.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Correct decisions of the starting solution should not be changed.
 Therefore, changes should remain within the corridor around the target
 solution, with the distance to the start solution.
 Punishment should be made in correlation to the size of the corridor.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
For MDPs: The area where the difference between the start and target solution
 increases can be crucial, as the effect often only becomes apparent later.
 In terms of regression, however, this area is not particularly evaluated.
 In chess, for example, this first deviation would be the indicator for
 a blunder, which could not be corroded even later.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The goal of the combined regression error is still to minimise the distance
 to the target solution - only those solutions that require less behavioural
 change should be preferred.
\begin_inset Foot
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
Let's say we cook eggs for 10 minutes and a target cooking professional
 for 5 minutes.
 When considering whether we should cook our eggs for 3 minutes and 7, 7
 minutes would be preferable as an interim solution, because the extent
 of the changes to our already known cooking behaviour is less.
\end_layout

\end_inset

 In the evolutionary found candidates not only a genetic difference can
 be determined with the TED, it is also possible to calculate the phenotypic
 difference as regression error.
 This means that not only the difference to the target solution plays a
 role, but also how far from the starting solution it was necessary to deviate.
 For security reasons, it may be of great interest that the changes are
 seen as an approximation from the known to the black box, without unnecessarily
 deviating from the known or overshooting the mark.
 One possibility of implementation is a third dimension on the Pareto front.
 Another way of combining classical regression with relative regression
 to Origin is also shown and tested below.
\end_layout

