\end_layout

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The following regression formula was therefore tested, which evaluates the
 resulting 4 areas differently and can be considered umdependent on the
 normal regression error.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
\begin_inset Formula 
\[
\sum|(y-\mathring{y})|-(\mathring{y}-\hat{y})
\]

\end_inset

 [xxx Frage: lambda? y antihut oder y kreis?]
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
In our case it was multiplied by a factor of 
\begin_inset Formula $\lambda=0.1$
\end_inset

 and added to the normal regression error.
\end_layout

