\begin_layout Standard
Runs with 
\begin_inset Formula $\lambda=1$
\end_inset

 did not find any pareto candidates whatsoever.
 With a multiplication factor of 0.1 candidates were found, but no statistically
 significant properties could be attested to them.
 Since in other experiments on regression the mixing of approaches always
 turned out to be too much interference with the error measure as a source
 of error, classifying further experiments on a third Pareto dimension looks
 promising (both regression errors correlate with each other).
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Mixing different paradigms is rarely a good idea, as this experiment has
 shown.
 For future implementations, it is recommended to implement a separate Paretofro
nt.
